WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.197
This table turns business questions into subquery contracts.

00:00:04.197 --> 00:00:07.077
One benchmark suggests a scalar.

00:00:07.077 --> 00:00:10.857
Membership in a returned list suggests IN.

00:00:10.857 --> 00:00:14.977
Existence of any matching row suggests EXISTS.

00:00:14.977 --> 00:00:20.627
At least one comparison suggests ANY, while every comparison suggests ALL.

00:00:20.627 --> 00:00:26.147
A per-row calculation often uses a correlated scalar.

00:00:26.147 --> 00:00:31.172
This translation from question to contract is the main skill of the module.

00:00:31.172 --> 00:00:35.567
A subquery has a contract: it returns a shape.

00:00:35.567 --> 00:00:40.772
A scalar subquery must return at most one value where it is used.

00:00:40.772 --> 00:00:48.067
Before writing syntax, predict whether the inner query returns one value, one column with many rows,

00:00:48.067 --> 00:00:54.888
or a table. Shape mistakes are easier to prevent than to debug after the query becomes large.
